## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to handle external dependency fragility, multi-tenant isolation, and production risk management. The question evaluates end-to-end instrumentation, resilience patterns, and practical operational procedures rather than theoretical knowledge.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end observability with OpenTelemetry
- Retry budgets with exponential backoff and jitter
- Circuit breakers with configurable thresholds and recovery
- Backpressure through token bucket rate limiting
- Idempotent retries with deduplication keys
- Progressive canary rollouts with automated rollback
- Incident runbooks and alerting thresholds
- SLO/SLI definition and percentile-based monitoring

## Code Example

```javascript
// Circuit breaker around identity provider
class CircuitBreaker {
  constructor(threshold = 5, timeout = 3000) {
    this.failureCount = 0;
    this.threshold = threshold;
    this.timeout = timeout;
    this.state = 'CLOSED';
    this.lastFailure = null;
  }

  async execute(operation) {
    if (this.state === 'OPEN') {
      if (Date.now() - this.lastFailure > this.timeout) {
        this.state = 'HALF_OPEN';
      } else {
        throw new Error('Circuit breaker is OPEN');
      }
    }

    try {
      const result = await operation();
      this.onSuccess();
      return result;
    } catch (error) {
      this.onFailure();
      throw error;
    }
  }

  onSuccess() {
    this.failureCount = 0;
    this.state = 'CLOSED';
  }

  onFailure() {
    this.failureCount++;
    this.lastFailure = Date.now();
    if (this.failureCount >= this.threshold) {
      this.state = 'OPEN';
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to handle multi-region routing faults and basic SRE tooling without outsourcing to advanced chaos scenarios.

## Key Concepts

- Regional observability: latency, error rate, saturation per region
- Alerting: region-specific thresholds
- Traffic control: region-aware routing and small canaries
- Rollback: quick gateway reversion and regional validation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lightweight region-aware retry example (conceptual)
async function routeRequest(regionMap, path){
  const region = selectHealthyRegion(regionMap);
  const res = await fetch(`https://${region}${path}`);
  if(!res.ok) throw new Error('Region failed');
  return res;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate that the incident is resolved after rollback?
- What non-functional tests would you run before promoting a region back to full traffic?

## Why This Is Asked

This evaluates a candidate's ability to design resilient, multi-region metrics pipelines that can withstand regional failures while maintaining data integrity and SLAs.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-region ingestion architecture with blast radius containment
- Per-tenant quotas, token-bucket throttling, and bounded local buffering
- Idempotent writes with deterministic IDs and backpressure signaling
- Circuit breakers and automated regional failover mechanisms
- Observability metrics: ingress latency, drop rate, max replay delay
- Adaptive sampling for surge handling

## Code Example

```javascript
// pseudo-code for idempotent write with backpressure
function writeWithBackpressure(metric) {
  const id = generateDeterministicId(metric);
  if (isBackpressureActive()) {
    bufferLocally(metric);
    return;
  }
  return idempotentWrite(id, metric);
}
```
